With the vision (image/video) path, chat.prepare can refuse with .capacity
(waiting for / restarting the vision helper). Run.fail sent every structured
refusal as 400, so a transient capacity refusal came back as
"400 invalid_request_error" and clients kept resending instead of retrying.
Send the kind's own status: .capacity is 503, .request/.context_length stay 400.

diff --git a/zig/src/server/openai.zig b/zig/src/server/openai.zig
--- a/zig/src/server/openai.zig
+++ b/zig/src/server/openai.zig
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@
         const a = r.a;
         const kind_ok = cx.kind != .other and cx.kind != .server;
         const body = (if (kind_ok) errorBody(a, cx, field) else errorOther(a, cx.message)) catch return;
-        r.out.vt.reply(r.out.ctx, if (kind_ok) 400 else 500, wrapError(a, body) catch return);
+        r.out.vt.reply(r.out.ctx, if (kind_ok) cx.status() else 500, wrapError(a, body) catch return);
     }
 
     /// A reply that ended before anything was sent: a refusal's 400, a failure's 500, nothing when the client left.
